  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I was wondering if this compromise to the parameter bit limit was ever considered. I am even more eager to ask with a lot of users resorting to VRCFury's FX animator solution to \"compress\" parameters (which works wonders but adds more cpu work).\n\nPriority / Non-priority bits.\n\nThis way you can be generous with the maximum bits on an avatar, but still conserve network traffic. 256 bits can be the limit for priority bits; parameters that need to be frequently updated (face tracking, osc, etc). Every parameter not selected as \"priority\" can be slowly synced when loaded or when their values change (sliders, toggles, etc), but the maximum total bits will be 512 or another amount. On the avatar parameter list, users can choose which parameters they want to be prioritized.\n\nAnd of course this is coming from someone who doesn't understand VRChat's backend or networking, but I wanted to throw the idea out there in the possibility it wasn't explored. Thank you!",
